Usage: SET COLORIZE_CHANNELS [ON|OFF|TOGGLE]
  When ON (the default), every channel name the client displays is
  shown in a colour picked deterministically from the channel name
  itself. A given channel always gets the same colour, so it looks
  the same in joins, parts, topic lines, the channel list, WHO
  output and the status bar. The colour is computed from a hash of
  the name (case is ignored).

  The colours are drawn from a fixed palette chosen for legibility
  on dark terminals. Colouring only wraps the channel
  name itself; surrounding text is left untouched.

  Colours are only visible when SET DISPLAY_ANSI is ON; with ANSI
  display OFF the colour codes are stripped and names show plain.

  Use SET COLORIZE_WARP to shift the whole colour assignment if you
  do not like the colour a particular channel was given.

See Also:
  SET COLORIZE_NICKS
  SET COLORIZE_WARP
  SET DISPLAY_ANSI
